1 The sequence $\left\{(-1)^{n}\right\}$ is a sequence of equal variances;
2 If $\left\{a_{n}\right\}$ is a sequence of equal variances, then $\left\{a_{n}^{2}\right\}$ is an arithmetic sequence;
3 If $\left\{a_{n}\right\}$ is a sequence of equal variances, then $\left\{a_{k n}\right\}\left(k \in \mathbf{N}^{*}, k\right.$ is a constant) is also a sequence of equal variances;
4 If $\left\{a_{n}\right\}$ is both a sequence of equal variances and an arithmetic sequence, then the sequence is a constant sequence.
