$3 a_{k n}^{2}-a_{k(n-1)}^{2}=a_{k n}^{2}-a_{k n-1}^{2}+a_{k n-1}^{2}-a_{k n-2}^{2}+\cdots+a_{k n-k+1}^{2}-a_{k(n-1)}^{2}=k p$ meets the definition;
4 If the sequence $\left\{a_{n}\right\}$ satisfies $a_{n}^{2}-a_{n-1}^{2}=p, a_{n}-a_{n-1}=d$ (where $d$ is a constant):
If $d=0$, it is clear that $\left\{a_{n}\right\}$ is a constant sequence;
If $d \neq 0$, then dividing the two equations yields $a_{n}+a_{n-1}=\frac{p}{d}$, so $a_{n}=\frac{d^{2}+p}{2 d}$ (a constant), meaning $\left\{a_{n}\right\}$ is a constant sequence.
